[tools/validator] Reference validator and canonical serializer (reviewing) @dispatch(mechanical)
Files: crates/grimoire/src/parser.rs, projection.rs, serialize.rs, validate.rs, cut.rs, evaluate.rs, and the focused/end-to-end Rust fixtures.
Implement the reference parser, structural validator, cut extractor, canonical serializer, and the separately scoped static projection evaluator for the reviewed Grimoire prototype. The current prototype covers bundled descriptions, standalone layers, schema documents, addressed description selection, closed values, extensions, projection structure, recursive group targets, chained finalized decorations, address/scoping/locality checks, schema validation, cuts, opaque preservation, and serializer fixpoints. It is checked against the specification and recorded prototype decisions; unresolved schema-use authority and custom-schema extension ordering remain explicit follow-up boundaries.
Accept: The complete current Rust suite passes; valid document forms parse and serialize canonically; structural and schema failures identify check, location, and relevant identifier; successful cuts revalidate; non-cuts report C12; unknown extension data survives unchanged; projection evaluation remains static and does not bind to runtime execution.
-> grammar/review
-> tools/validator/conformance
> 2026-08-27: The coherence pass corrected canonical collection normalization, group-target expansion, chained finalized-decoration propagation, site-blind structural equality, and addressed description selection.
> 2026-08-27: Layer schema-use authority and generic custom schema ordering for extension values remain design/API gaps; the prototype does not claim those contracts are settled.
