[layers/cost] Cost layer (reviewing)
Files: crates/grimoire/src/cost.rs, crates/grimoire/src/lib.rs, crates/grimoire/tests/cost.rs, and proposals/cost-layer.md.
Provide a static cost analysis boundary with constant, addressed-axis, sum, and product expressions. Evaluate only with caller-supplied positive axis extents and checked u64 arithmetic. Assign expressions to visible addressed elements, then recursively aggregate priced leaves through visible groups; repeated members, cycles, absent elements, missing prices, and overflow fail visibly. Keep this algebra outside the current text grammar until symbolic projection syntax has a separate contract. Do not infer FLOPs, bytes, sparsity, precision widths, hardware throughput, or runtime behavior from labels or topology.
Accept: V-JEPA-style axis products, bridge/projector terms, low-bit variant terms, and group totals evaluate deterministically; missing symbolic inputs and malformed aggregation fail visibly; cost values do not participate in structural selection.
-> core/freeze
-> projlang/spec
-> schemas/axes
-> schemas/shapes
> 2026-08-27: The first cost algebra is a host-side static analysis API over an evaluated reprojection, not a new grammar/value constructor.
> 2026-08-27: Axis terms resolve only from explicit positive extent bindings; no semantic meaning is inferred from axis names.
> 2026-08-27: Group totals sum explicitly priced leaves and reject unpriced leaves, duplicate members, missing elements, and cycles rather than returning partial totals.
> 2026-08-27: Cost units remain authored and unitless until a later convention names a FLOP, memory, or hardware interpretation.
