[information/bayesian-update] Update channel posteriors from observations (reviewing)
Files: crates/grimoire/src/information.rs and crates/grimoire/tests/information.rs.
Replace purely caller-weighted channel scenarios with an evidence-driven finite categorical posterior path. Define a validated prior over channel hypotheses, update it from finite source/target observations using likelihood, and expose posterior channel weights, credible intervals, and threshold decision probabilities. Keep the prior, likelihood, posterior, and information estimand visible; do not conflate posterior uncertainty with Bayesian mutual information.
Accept: A supplied prior updates reproducibly from observations; empty evidence preserves the prior; impossible observations fail visibly; posterior weights normalize; posterior mutual-information and retention summaries produce credible intervals and threshold probabilities; prior sensitivity remains inspectable.
-> information/channel-contract
-> information/claims
-> information/finite-calculus
> 2026-08-27: ChannelObservation records finite source/target transitions; ChannelPosterior::update reweights explicit hypotheses in log space and reports posterior collapse when all hypotheses assign zero likelihood.
